<title>USA: American Radio to buy stations for $90 mln.</title>
<headline>American Radio to buy stations for $90 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Radio Systems Corp said it had reached an agreement to acquire radio stations WWMX-FM and WOCT-FM in Baltimore from Capitol Broadcasting Co for $90 million.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement late on Wednesday that WWMX would be acquired for about $60 million and WOCT bought for about $30 million. Consummation of the transaction is subject to the approval of the Federal Communications Commission.</p>
<p>American Radio Systems owns WQSR-FM and WBMD-AM in Baltimore.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
</text>
